/////////////////////////////////////////////////

Key Architectural Decisions
Security (No XSS): We have explicitly eliminated localStorage for tokens. On the Web, we use HttpOnly cookies for the refresh token. The accessToken lives only in memory (a volatile variable). If the user refreshes, they must hit /refresh to get a new access token. This is the gold standard for banking and high-security apps.

API-First Approach: By keeping the accessToken inside the Authorization: Bearer header, your backend remains agnostic of the client. Whether it’s a React Native app or a browser, the validation logic (middleware.ts) looks exactly the same.

Device-Awareness: Every login creates an entry in a sessions collection in CouchDB. This allows us to track deviceName, platform (iOS/Android/Web), and createdAt. Revoking a session is as simple as deleting that document in CouchDB.

Token Rotation: Every time /refresh is called, we issue a new refresh token. This allows us to detect token theft; if a leaked refresh token is reused, we can immediately invalidate the entire session chain.


